## Deterministic Global IDs

IDs must be deterministic across reruns and globally unique across all PDFs.

- Compute `doc_key` deterministically from PDF bytes (e.g., SHA-256)
- Create canonical string IDs and convert to UUID deterministically (e.g., UUIDv5):
  - `lc:curriculum:{doc_key}:framework`
  - `lc:curriculum:{doc_key}:sfi:{role}:{path_or_code}:{normalized_text_hash}`
  - `lc:curriculum:{doc_key}:lc:{source_sfi_id}:{split_index_or_hash}`
- Preserve local codes when present (metadata and/or part of canonical keys)

Strict rule: Never use random UUIDs as stable identifiers.

